    "summary": "Alligator jam, tight Dancin' In The Street & soaring Lovelight sequence",
    "blurb": "Highlights include a scorching Alligator jam that launches an hour‑plus second set, a funky Dancin' In The Street jam and the electric Turn On Your Lovelight > Not Fade Away > Turn On Your Lovelight sequence. Pigpen’s organ adds texture on acoustic numbers like The Frozen Logger, while Bill Kreutzmann’s drumming drives the jams.",
    "review": "June 6 1970 at the Fillmore West captures a Grateful Dead in full exploratory mode. After an unassuming first set, the band erupts with a monster Alligator jam that sets the tone for a second set packed with seamless segues – China Cat Sunflower into I Know You Rider, Good Lovin' into a thunderous Drums‑New Orleans stretch, and the dazzling Turn On Your Lovelight > Not Fade Away > Turn On Your Lovelight sandwich. Garcia’s lead work soars on Alligator, Morning Dew and the China‑Rider transition, while Bill Kreutzmann (and Mickey Hart) provide a powerful rhythmic backbone that propels the jams. The acoustic fragment shines with Pigpen’s organ texture and Bob Weir delivering some of his strongest vocals on The Frozen Logger and Friend Of The Devil. Overall the show is a rare snapshot of the Dead balancing tight musicianship, improvisational firepower, and soulful Americana.",
